  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hawaiki Nui Regional Submarine Cable Branching Units - Pacific - Telecommunications</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reliable, cost-effective international submarine cable connections can have a significant impact on a country&#x2019;s security as well as social and economic development. While many Pacific Island countries have, or will soon have, one submarine cable connection, opportunities for cost-effective submarine cable connections to remote Pacific Island Countries for the purposes of providing a first submarine cable connection, or redundancy, are limited. The proposed Hawaiki Nui cable (Nui), to be ready for service in 2027, offers close proximity connectivity options to the following jurisdictions - Timor-Leste, Papua New Guinea (PNG) and Solomon Islands.</narrative>
  </description>
